    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d24-a8">

                <pb facs="0439" n="429" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv07/pg429"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure 2]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>G. H. Q.</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1919-07-20">20 July,
                    1919</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">Copy of Telegram</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">No. 3454</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">From The Commander in Chief of the Allied Armies</p>
                <p rendition="#flush">To General Nudant, President of C. I. P. A., Cologne.</p>
                <list>
                    <item>Firstly: The Head of the British Delegation at the Peace Conference
                        informs me, that General von der Goltz has no knowledge of the powers given
                        to General Gough by the Entente.</item>
                    <pb facs="0440" n="430" xml:id="pg430"/>
                    <item>Secondly: Repeat the instructions contained in my former telegrams to the
                        German Armistice Committee, and order them to give the necessary orders to
                        the German Commander in the Baltic Regions without delay.</item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Foch</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
